# image/pins.env: every pin of the fence image in ONE place (plan §3 U1a). image/build.sh reads this
# file and passes each line to the Dockerfile as --build-arg, so the Dockerfile has no pin of its own
# and an unset one fails the build. It exists so that bumping Claude Code or the base is one reviewed
# diff here, and so a pin can be compared with the vendor's manifest (image/build.sh --check-pins).
# Plain KEY=VALUE, no quotes, no shell. Source of the Claude Code numbers: the stable channel's
# manifest.json of the release bucket below (glibc builds, NOT -musl).
# SNAPSHOT: the snapshot.debian.org date apt installs from, so two builds of these pins hold the same
# package bytes (it is the date the BASE image itself was built from, read from its debian.sources).
# PYTHON3_MINIMAL_VERSION, LIBPYTHON3_STDLIB_VERSION: the client layer (/opt/ccf, plan C3) is stdlib-only Python 3 and
# the fence has no other interpreter. python3-minimal alone has no `json`, so the stdlib library is pinned with it; the
# versions are what the SNAPSHOT above offers (tests/image-test.sh checks python3 --version and `import json`).
# BASE_DIFF_ID: the diff id (hash of the uncompressed layer) of the base image's one layer; tests/image-test.sh
# skips ONLY the layer with this id when it scans layers for credentials (the base is pinned by digest,
# and a library in it carries sample strings). Not a build arg.
BASE_DIFF_ID=sha256:1d7b9dd8778ebc4d9bf2f64436dd358640718cb349f5640b33bebaea4ffd62c2
BASE=docker.io/library/debian:bookworm-slim@sha256:734a72b3d6142a71993b4bc580ca01d8ca687f77a2c422d96a961d3376b179bc
CLAUDE_VERSION=2.1.311
CLAUDE_URL_BASE=https://storage.googleapis.com/claude-code-dist-86c565f3-f756-42ad-8dfa-d59b1c096819/claude-code-releases
CLAUDE_SHA256_AMD64=86dc1fcc69498159eaf15f446613e847010f9036bfbbdffd4c49350be8489ada
CLAUDE_SHA256_ARM64=2e2496c9a8065df93acb0fca2d341f59a6b8777649b2e025ab8c9bcd5eef61f3
SNAPSHOT=20261104T212339Z
PYTHON3_MINIMAL_VERSION=3.11.2-1+b1
LIBPYTHON3_STDLIB_VERSION=3.11.2-6+deb12u9
